{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/281569-pacts-interim-period","id":281569,"title":"Pacts & Interim period","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-14T16:01:51-07:00","id":281569,"title":"Pacts & Interim period","content":"So the question arose from discussing Pacts. What happens to the subjects of pacts in the interim period between spending Cover Experiences and acquiring them? For instance, if I pact for someone's wife, and they're a major part of their life, I gain those 3 Cover Experiences to spend. But what if, after getting him to sign the pact, I don't immediately spend those Cover Experiences? I haven't yet integrated his wife into my Cover. Does my side of the pact only get enacted when I do?<br /> <br /> Does he immediately cease being married to his wife when he signs that Pact? If that's the case, what does she think during the intermittent period? Does she remain married to her husband until I integrate her into my Cover, then suddenly she's married to me?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T16:26:37-07:00","id":281602,"title":"","content":"Theoretically? They still apply to one of your covers, it just that there's not enough relevant detail to make it worth a point-you need more information to make a noticeable increase in your personal infrastructure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T17:09:26-07:00","id":281646,"title":"","content":"I would say it still counts as part of your Cover, it's just not metaphysically integrated into it enough to bolster it and solidify it yet. Maybe gaining the Cover Experiences is represented by the Pact, but spending the Cover Experiences is represented by the Demon interacting and integrating that stuff into their Cover in an active (and not just passive) way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T11:57:44-07:00","id":282564,"title":"","content":"The way I would run it for my games is that each facet of a pact traded away by a mortal has essentially three types of owners: the human who traded it away, the holder who has it for a transistory period (usually the cover who made the deal in the first place, though in my game pact parts can also be traded away so the holder can change a few times) and the beneficiary who integrates it permanently into his or her cover by spending the beats or XP.<br /> <br /> The reason why I went with this method is I wanted a solid, easy answer for who counts as, say, a traded woman's husband; maintenance of these pacts in transit is supposed to be easily taken care of with a phone call or something every once in a while since it really shouldn't matter. If players try to abuse this rule to get the benefits of a pact over multiple covers and give me the headache I was trying to avoid entirely, I can only imagine how aggravated I'm going to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}